  "name": "Creation Storage",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/melee/blood-slash-foam-red.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 11th level, you can now store a creation in an object. Whenever you finish a long rest, you can touch one simple or martial weapon or one item that you can use as a creation focus, and you store a creation in it, choosing a creation from the gadgeteer creation list that requires 1 action to cast (you needn't have it prepared) and be of a level equal to half your proficiency bonus (rounded up).</p>\n<p>While holding the object, a creature can take an action to produce the creation's effect from it, using your creation ability modifier. If the creation requires concentration, the creature must concentrate.</p>\n<p>The creation stays in the object until it's been used a number of times equal to twice your Intelligence modifier (minimum of twice) or until you use this feature again to store a creation in an object.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
